From 1b21215d5d4b5c63dc308443da4eca5ce80fb5ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 05:58:57 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cdp): a page's Page events reach every session attached
 to it that enabled Page

Page events went only to the session whose command caused them, so a second
client watching a tab (a live view next to the agent driving it) never saw
the frameNavigated, lifecycle or load events of navigations the other session
drove, and had to poll for them. Chrome sends a page's Page events to every
session of that page with the domain enabled. Sessions that call Page.enable
are tracked (Page.disable, detach and page close forget them), and the events
leaving the connection are fanned out to them, except screencast frames,
which belong to each screencast's own ack loop.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
---
 crates/obscura-cdp/src/dispatch.rs       | 87 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 crates/obscura-cdp/src/domains/page.rs   |  9 +++
 crates/obscura-cdp/src/domains/target.rs |  1 +
 crates/obscura-cdp/src/server.rs         |  6 +-
 4 files changed, 100 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

